#: modules/core/core.php:175
msgid "Should we import all the rows from external sources always?"
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:176
msgid "By default, when you configure an ongoing import from Google Sheets or from a FTP server, we import all the rows from the external location the first time, but the next imports will only include the modified rows which provides multiple benefits: the imports will finish much faster and you will use fewer server resources on your WordPress site. But you can enable this option if you want to process all the rows always, maybe because you're going to add duplicate rows in Google Sheets/FTP and you don't want them to be excluded."
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:182
msgid "Imports: How long can an import batch run before we consider it as stuck?"
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:183
msgid "If you leave this empty, we'll consider the batch that's been in progress for more than 15 minutes as \"stuck\" and consider it eligible for a retry if it's possible to retry. But if your server is configured to allow batches to run for longer, the batch might be running correctly during our check. You should enter a number higher than the max execution time set in the PHP settings. Enter 0 to disable the retries."
msgstr ""

