#: modules/core/core.php:694
msgid "This means the job was successfully executed and it won't run again. If this is a real-time sync, the first full run has been completed and it's listening and monitoring for changes right now."
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:695
msgid "This means the job will no longer be used for anything, it's archived for historical purposes only and it can be deleted once you no longer need to review its log."
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:696
msgid "This means that the job is running at this moment, it's processing all its related batches."
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:697
msgid "This means that the job has been cancelled and removed from the schedule, it won't run again and it won't be used for anything"
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:698
msgid "This means that there was an error when executing this job and it was marked as failed so you review the log to find out what happened, you can edit the job and manually schedule it to run again when you fix the issue."
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:699
msgid "The job was temporarily paused and removed from the schedule. It will not run on its originally scheduled date but can be resumed later. If the original date hasn't passed, it will execute on the original date when resumed. If the original date has already passed, it will be rescheduled to run at the time of resumption. If the job was paused during a batch, the current batch will continue to be processed. However, the next batch will not be processed until the job is resumed."
msgstr ""

#: modules/core/core.php:700
msgid "The job will be returned to its previous state before it was archived. If the previous state was scheduled and the date has not passed yet, it will be automatically rescheduled to run on the same date. However, if the previously scheduled date has already passed, it will run immediately. If the job was archived during execution, it will resume from where it left off. If the job was a real-time sync, it will resume its function of listening and monitoring for changes."
msgstr ""

