#: modules/imports/external-source-abstract.php:408
msgid "Move items to the trash in WordPress when they are deleted in the external source?"
msgstr ""

#: modules/imports/external-source-abstract.php:408
msgid "By default, if a row has been removed in your external file, the item won't be deleted or moved to the trash in WordPress. We delete from WordPress only when you set the \"Status\" column with a value \"delete\" in the external file or move to the trash when you set \"Status\" with a value \"trash\". You can activate this option if you want to move to the trash in WordPress all the rows that were deleted in the external source file. We move them to the trash instead of fully deleting to give you the chance to restore if you make a mistake."
msgstr ""

